      "text": "First card can be 6 in 4 ways (since there are 4 sixes in a deck of 52 cards). So probability of it obtained first time is (1/52)\nNow, total number of ways of 3 cards left after first is drawn is (51)!.\nSo, probability of the third card now being a queen is (4/52)= (1/13).\nTherefore, Total probability of the first card being 6 and second being qyeen is (1/52)*(1/13)=(1/676)\n\nQuestion: Tom drives 1000 miles a month.  Every 50 miles, he stops to get gas.  He also stops once every 2 months for oil changes which costs $200.  He also stops twice a year for maintenance which costs $50 each.  He pays $4 per gallon of gas and gas is $3 per gallon.  How much does he spend on driving a year? Let's write a Python program. # define the constants\nmiles_per_month = 1000\ncost_per_gallon_of_gas = 4\ncost_per_gallon = 3\noil_change_frequency = 2\noil_change_cost = 200\nmaintenance_frequency = 2\nmaintenance_cost = 50\nmonths_in_year = 12\n\n# calculate the gas usage\ngallons_used_per_month = miles_per_month / 50\ngallons_used_per_year = gallons_used_per_month * months_in_year\n\n# calculate the cost of gas\ncost_of_gas_per_year = gallons_used_per_year * cost_per_gallon\n\n# calculate the cost of oil changes\noil_change_cost_per_year = oil_change_frequency * oil_change_cost\n\n# calculate the cost of maintenance\nmaintenance_cost_per_year = maintenance_frequency * maintenance_cost\n\n# calculate the total cost\ntotal_cost_per_year = cost_of_gas_per_year + oil_change_cost_per_year + maintenance_cost_per_year\nprint(total_cost_per_year)",
